       ```js
       app.post('/posts', s3uploader.single('image'), createPost)
       ```
       So whenever we do the post request, then s3 will generate the the middleware for us. That middleware expext the file from us a single file. The key of the file should be image. This key uniqly identify the incoming input. 
       - so postman mai form ke through ham request send kar sakte hai like key: Image, value : System se image dedo

       Why having the callback and we passing null in multerConfig.js. 
       Express follow a pattern , error first callback. Express says that if we are having callback and it has to handle somekind of error. Then error should be the first parameter of that callback. 
        - See the fs module -> read
        - If pass null then it denotes that there is no error at all. 

